<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/14th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Rovine</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1395">1395</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Rovine was fought on 17 May 1395 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mircea-the-elder">Mircea the Elder of Wallachia</a> and the Ottoman sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bayezid-i">Bayezid I</a>, whose army included Serbian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a>. The Serbian lords <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-marko">Marko Mrnjavčević</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konstantin-dragas">Konstantin Dragaš</a> were killed. The outcome is disputed, but Mircea held the field and Wallachia preserved its autonomy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-rovine.jpg" alt="Battle of Rovine" width="320" height="200" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dimitrie Papazoglu · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Rovine.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
